Author: AnchorAI <54788874-AnchorAI@users.noreply.replit.com>
Date:   Wed Mar 18 08:48:02 2026 -0400

    Task #12: Visit status inline spinner feedback
    
    Updated the route builder's stop action menu to show a spinner
    only on the specific menu item that was clicked, rather than
    showing spinners on all menu items for the same visit.
    
    Changes in routes-page.tsx:
    - Added `updatingVisitStatus` state alongside `updatingVisitId`
      to track which status transition is in progress
    - Updated visitStatusMutation to set/clear both states
    - Updated DraggableStop component to accept `updatingVisitStatus`
      prop and conditionally show Loader2 spinner only on the menu
      item matching the active status change
    - Updated the quick-complete button to show spinner only when
      the "completed" status is being set (not for skip/cancel)
    - Updated the dropdown trigger button (MoreVertical) to show
      a spinner when a non-complete status change is pending
      (since the menu closes after clicking)
    - Threaded `updatingVisitStatus` prop through RouteCard to
      DraggableStop in both route cards and unassigned panel
    - Other stops' action menus remain fully interactive

